/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An ad hoc network has no fixed infrastructure: every node forwards packets for the others, so distant nodes reach each other in several hops.
   - Road crashes kill about 1.19 million people a year worldwide, according to the WHO's 2023 global status report, most of them in low- and middle-income countries such as India.
   - VANETs differ from general mobile ad hoc networks (MANETs): nodes move fast, so links last seconds; motion follows roads, so it is predictable; vehicles have plenty of battery power and space; position and time come from GNSS; and the netwo
   - Topology-based routing finds and stores a path.
   - Geocast sends a message to every vehicle inside a target area, such as 1 km behind a crash; it suppresses the broadcast storm by letting only the farthest receiver rebroadcast, or by random waiting.
*/
