/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In the USA the DSRC band was 5.850 to 5.925 GHz, seven 10 MHz channels: one control channel (CCH), channel 178, and six service channels (SCH).
   - The 802.11p physical layer uses OFDM, like 802.11a, but with the clock halved: 10 MHz channels instead of 20 MHz, so every symbol is twice as long (8 µs).
   - The common safety message is the basic safety message (BSM) of SAE J2735: position, speed, heading, acceleration, brake status and vehicle size, sent about ten times a second, typically 200 to 400 bytes with its security data.
*/
