/* book exam traps: 802.11p uses 10 MHz channels, not the 20 MHz of 802.11a, so its symbols are twice as long and its rates are half. | WAVE is not another name for 802.11p: 802.11p is only the MAC and physical layer; WAVE is the IEEE 1609 layers above it. | The 100 ms sync interval is the channel-switching rhythm of 1609.4; it does not mean only one BSM fits in it. | 3 to 27 Mbit/s is the raw physical rate; delivered throughput in a crowded channel is much lower. */
